# Trivy ignore file for Purl
#
# WIRED INTO CI: .github/workflows/ci.yml passes this file to every
# aquasecurity/trivy-action step (`trivyignores: .trivyignore`).
#
# The following scans FAIL the build on HIGH/CRITICAL:
#   - security-fs job    : filesystem scan (vuln + secret)
#   - build-test job     : image scan of the PR-built image (vuln only)
#   - build-and-push job : image scan BEFORE the push to Docker Hub (vuln only)
#
# Why the image scans run vuln-only (no secret scanner):
# the image bundles third-party CPAN libraries that ship sample keys inside
# their POD/tests (Crypt::JWT, Crypt::PK::{RSA,ECC,DSA,Ed25519}, and
# Mojo::IOLoop's built-in test server.key). Those are upstream docs/test
# fixtures, not our secrets, and we cannot strip them from the dependency.
# Secret detection for OUR code is not weakened: the security-fs job scans
# the repository with scanners: vuln,secret and fails on any finding.
#
# Add a CVE ID below only to accept a vulnerability we cannot fix
# (e.g. no upstream patch yet). Every entry needs a reason + a date so
# this list gets re-reviewed instead of growing forever.
#
# Note: scans run with `ignore-unfixed: true`, so CVEs with no available
# fix are already excluded and do NOT need an entry here.
#
# Format: one CVE ID per line. Optional expiry: CVE-2024-12345 exp:2026-12-31
#
# Example:
# CVE-2024-67890 exp:2026-09-01
#   reason: base image perl:5.40-slim-bookworm, fix pending upstream
#   owner: devops, added: 2026-07-14
